cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or refer to its results, please cite the accompanying article and this repository."
title: "PhysaRoute: Physarum conductance dynamics for reliable, energy-aware routing in healthcare wireless body area networks (reference simulator)"
type: software
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-28
authors:
  - family-names: "Azzawi"
    given-names: "Mustafa A."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9360-4174"
    email: "mazzawi1991@gmail.com"
  - family-names: "Abdulhussein"
    given-names: "Ansam A."
  - family-names: "Hassan"
    given-names: "Rosilah"
repository-code: "https://github.com/azzawi91/PhysaRoute"
license: "LicenseRef-AllRightsReserved"
abstract: >
  Discrete-event simulator for adaptive routing in IEEE 802.15.6 wireless body area networks:
  a measured-statistics body channel, CSMA/CA MAC, first-order radio energy, the PhysaRoute
  protocol (Physarum tube-conductance dynamics with an advertised potential field, energy- and
  criticality-aware tube length and end-to-end confirmed reinforcement) and eight baseline
  protocols (AODV, M-ATTEMPT, SIMPLE, ACO-WBAN, PSO-Relay, GWO-Relay, QL-WBAN, QoS-2C), with the
  experiment driver, statistics and figure pipeline that reproduce every reported number.
keywords:
  - wireless body area network
  - healthcare IoT
  - bio-inspired routing
  - Physarum polycephalum
  - IEEE 802.15.6
  - discrete-event simulation
